UniXNU 3fd6a3c: source storage without a userdata root ([storage] root = "none"), gap G2 of macOS-Pad-6

build-sheng-source-storage.py builds the arm64e UFS adapter only for a board whose roots are signed images in userdata:
it requires a policy directory, manifests whose verification matches the profile's root images, and links their owner
anchor. A board that mounts no root from userdata (macOS-Pad-6 keeps Android's userdata as it is) has none of those.

With board.toml [storage] root = "none" the kernel step exports UNIXNU_SOURCE_STORAGE_ROOT=none and the recipe skips
the policy directory and manifests, writes an empty policy bundle and links an all-zero 395-byte anchor, which vr_open
accepts nothing with: NativeUfs publishes no verified root window. Everything else (headers, the deferred
IOBlockStorageDevice metaclass, NativeUfs with the board's SoC switch from 0001, the device package sources) is built
as before. A board other than sheng also gets its package searched under kits/<kit> ([board] kit, exported as
UNIXNU_KIT): the recipe looked only in package/ and kits/sheng. Applies after 0001. Not yet built: the recipe runs on the macOS runner only (kernel-build.yml
[storage-build]).

